features/sea-compact/world-task.md:5:Make the slice sea compact and dense, so ships meet. Today the map is 224 × 208 tiles and 99.2 % open sea: four small islands sit in its corners, and with a 10-tile sight radius players rarely see each other. The operator's playtest verdict: "a denser map, and reduce the scale". Shrink the world, slow the ships so §3's travel times still hold, fill the sea with obstacles and landmarks that funnel routes together, and draw everything larger so the sight circle fits the screen.
